module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.an_untyped_empty_map_fold_seed_is_emitted_with_a_bare_alias_head

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data an_untyped_empty_map_fold_seed_is_emitted_with_a_bare_alias_head: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "an_untyped_empty_map_fold_seed_is_emitted_with_a_bare_alias_head" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "E0107 on gunbc#14084: the seed-emitter renders an untyped `empty_map()` in a fold `init` position with the type alias expanded to its bare head: `fold(names, init: empty_map(), f: fn(acc, name) { map_insert(acc, name, qualified_name_snoc(qn: p, segment: name)) })` returning Map<Symbol, QualifiedName> emitted `v1_rt::rc_empty_map::<Symbol, Rc<FreeMonoid>>()`, dropping FreeMonoid's argument (QualifiedName = FreeMonoid<Symbol>); rustc refuses `E0107 missing generics for type alias std_algebra::FreeMonoid` at stage0/src/v2_compiler_resolve.rs:3337 (CI receipts: head d948d9a and e64a435). A typed `let seed: Map<Symbol, QualifiedName> = empty_map()` emitted `rc_empty_map::<_, _>()` and compiled."

    "INVALID STATE: a well-typed .dag fold over an alias-typed map is accepted by the compiler and emitted as Rust that does not compile. HARM: the required emit-and-build job refuses (EmittedCompilerBuildFailed, floor_class=structural) on source the checker admitted, so the author must find a source shape the emitter happens to render; the refusal is loud, not silent."

    "RUNG FOUND AT: 1, mitigatable -- the failure is caught only by building the emitted crate. CEILING: 3, structurally guaranteed: the emitter renders an inferred type by its full application (alias expanded to FreeMonoid<Symbol>) or by a placeholder, never by the bare head. NEXT TRIGGER: the seed-emitter's type rendering for an inferred generic argument; owner tidy-swift-183 (queued after #14069, per clever-crane-830). WORKAROUND (labeled): src/v2/compiler/resolve.dag type_param_value_binders types its seed with a let; delete that let when the emitter renders the alias correctly."

    "STANDING (2026-10-16): REPRODUCED on main only in the self-host build. With the resolve.dag type_param_value_binders typed-let workaround deleted, //gunbc/instruments:self-host over v2.compiler.source_root_eval refuses E0107 at stage0/src/v2_compiler_resolve.rs:3371 on main's emitter; that is the discriminating RED. Two sites carry the bare head, both from the alias reference being projected to its resolved node FreeMonoid without its argument (child_type_node, env alias resolved_type): the seed turbofish rc_empty_map::<Symbol, Rc<FreeMonoid>>() and the fold lambda's acc annotation Rc<HashMap<Symbol, Rc<FreeMonoid>>>. Fix at the emitter's rendering of both (05_emit_rust type_node_carries_applicationless_parametric_head: a map type whose child renders a bare parametric head defers to ::<_, _>(), and the lambda acc type renders _); the typed-let workaround is deleted and the self-host build now executes the untyped seed. The four native-emission-controls cases (alias_empty_map_seed_*) are GUARDS, not discriminators: same-module, cross-module, real QualifiedName/Symbol and match-arm shapes all emit and compile on main, so they do not reproduce the self-host-only shape. REMAINING GAP, below ceiling (interim, operator-approved compensation): the emitter rule above is a COMPENSATION at a symptom link, to be deleted by the follow-up. Root, probed on the self-host tree (a WIP attempt that routed type-argument rendering through the reference application and kept child children in the 04_resolve keyed-collection and single-element arms stayed red at the same site, 2026-10-17): v1 infer gives a value typed by a declared-return alias (qualified_name_snoc -> QualifiedName) as the alias EXPANSION, FreeMonoid with its Empty/Cons variant children and no application, rather than the reference QualifiedName; the Map<Symbol, V> built by map_insert over it therefore has a value node with no type argument anywhere, so no later link can recover it. Earliest unjustified boundary: infer producing the expansion for a declared-return alias. NEXT TRIGGER (capability): infer carries the reference (with its application) for a declared-return alias, after which the emitter rule and its predicates are deleted. That trigger is owned by work item adhoc-65526d74-43f (tidy-ant-251, Family A alias identity), whose test matrix gains a declared-return alias with type arguments; the compensation is deleted when that relation lands; the full attempt (rust_type_argument_node routing, resolve writer) is kept on branch session/jolly-bear-353-e0107-wip for that follow-up. The alias_empty_map_seed_* fixtures are source-identical to the failing shape yet pass on main, so they are guards; a RED independent of the resolve.dag body needs a fixture run through the v1 seed emission, and that missing harness is part of the trigger.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: E0107 `missing generics for type alias` naming a std alias at a turbofish in an emitted file; the source holds an untyped empty_map()/empty collection in an init or argument position whose element type is an alias of a generic."
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
